# SQL's `SELECT` after a pipe: DS0105, with a fix to `project`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | SELECT customerId, amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..46
  PIPELINE@0..45
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    PROJECT_OP@20..45
      IDENT@20..26 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@27..37
        NAME_REF@27..37
          IDENT@27..37 "customerId"
      COMMA@37..38 ","
      WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@39..45
        NAME_REF@39..45
          IDENT@39..45 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@45..46 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `SELECT` is not an operator
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | SELECT customerId, amount
  |                     ^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: choose or compute columns with `project`: `project a, b`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | project customerId, amount
which parses without errors
